# Migration files are content-checksummed by src/db/migrate.ts and an applied file is immutable, so
# a CRLF checkout would drift EVERY applied migration against the one real database at once — and
# the only documented recovery for drift used to be a destructive reset. Pin the line endings so a
# checkout can never manufacture that.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, less severe: keep the whole tree consistent so diffs are about content.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
